<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenian shares end firm, Lek gains two percent.</title>
<headline>Slovenian shares end firm, Lek gains two percent.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenian shares closed 0.13 percent higher on Wednesday and traders said activity was dominated by month-end book balancing.</p>
<p>* The SBI index rose 1.69 points to 1,316.56.</p>
<p>* Overall 10 shares rose, four fell and 13 were untraded.</p>
<p>* Issue A of drug firm Lek rose 2.11 percent to 24,710 tolars on volume of 221 shares.</p>
<p>-- Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
</text>
